# Dependencies are vendored and committed (go mod vendor).
# No network needed after clone.

# Build artifacts
/bin/
/ze-*
/functional
# cache/ and tmp/ become checkout-specific symlinks through
# `./le scratch links-ensure`; Go skips those directory symlinks.
# See plan/spec-relocate-scratch-and-cache.md.
/cache
tmp/*
!tmp/go.mod

# Local backups
/backups/
# go test -c / benchmark binaries
*.test

# Build outputs (kernel, initrd, pxe, ipxe)
build/

# credentials database (generated by ze init)
database.zefs
etc/ze/database.zefs*

# Functional tests under development. A .ci in here is invisible to every suite
# and every repo-wide gate (see test/draft/README.md), so a half-written test can
# never redden `./le verify current mode full` or CI. Ignored rather than merely excluded: CI
# checks out git, so an ignored tree does not exist there at all, which makes the
# guarantee independent of every gate remembering to skip it.
# Promote with: mv test/draft/<suite>/<name>.ci test/<suite>/<name>.ci
#
# `test/draft/*`, NOT `test/draft/`: git does not descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so the negation below would never be evaluated and the README would
# be ignored too, leaving the convention undiscoverable from a fresh clone.
test/draft/*
!test/draft/README.md

# MRT data files (large, downloaded)
test/internet/*.gz
test/internet/*.bz2
test/internet/*.tmp

# Research output (large generated files)
docs/research/comparison/
docs/research/ze-vpp-plan.md
*-inlined.html

# Restricted-source reconstruction. Keep local and never commit.
rfc/full/iso-iec-10589.txt

# Coverage reports
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Mutation testing incremental cache (gomu hardcodes this cwd path)
.gomu_history.json


# macOS
.DS_Store

# Obsidian
.obsidian/

# Claude session state (lives in tmp/session/, covered by tmp/ ignore)
# Legacy locations kept for transition period:
.claude/session-state.md
.claude/session-state-*.md
.claude/.session-*
.claude/.compaction-detected
.claude/.compaction-detected-*
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Generated AI tool config (canonical sources: ai/skills/, ai/agents/,
# ai/INSTRUCTIONS.md)
# Regenerate with: ./le ai skills-sync
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.claude/skills/
.codex/skills/
.agents/skills/
.claude/agents/

test/perf/results/
bin/ze-perf-linux
# Cross-compiled ze binary staged into the IPsec interop Docker build context by
# `buildZe` in `internal/le/interoplab/ipsec`; regenerated each run.
test/interop-ipsec/ze-linux

# Runtime / scratch artifacts that leak into the working tree from running ze
/stderr
/stdout
screenlog.*
# The AAA audit trail a daemon started from the repository root appends to.
# One line per privileged action, with the actor and the remote address on it.
/ze.audit.jsonl
etc/ze/*.tmp
etc/ze/debug.zefs
# ddos-detect (and other plugins) persist rolling runtime state here; never commit it.
etc/ze/state/
internal/appliance/build/

# Appliance builddir lock for the ze module itself. Derived and duplicated: that
# module is only `replace ze => <repo root>`, so every line of its go.sum is
# already in the root go.sum. Tracking it created a second place to update on
# each dependency bump. The native appliance dependency resolver regenerates
# this file. The other gokrazy/ze/builddir go.sum files stay tracked because
# kernel dependencies that appear nowhere else.
gokrazy/ze/builddir/github.com/ze-software/ze/go.sum

# Derived documentation indexes, generated on demand and never committed.
# `./le docs-to-code update` and `./le docs-to-code index-update` write them
# from Go design headers and source anchors.
/ai/DOCS-TO-CODE.md
/ai/CODE-TO-DOCS.md
